# Roadmap Ideas Git Workflow

This worktree implements Brain roadmap tasks one at a time. Follow this loop unless the user says otherwise.

## Per-task loop

1. Sync: `git checkout main && git pull`
2. Branch: `git checkout -b feature/<task-slug>` (e.g. `feature/memory-receipts`)
3. Commit often — one logical change per commit
4. When satisfied: merge to `main` with `--no-ff` to preserve every commit and leave a clear task boundary
5. Delete the task branch after merge (optional)
6. Start the next task from updated `main`

## Commit messages

Use prefixes that map to the roadmap slice:

```
brain(receipts): persist gate reason on auxiliary memories
brain(summary): handle "what did you learn about me?" voice query
```

## Merge strategy

- Prefer `git merge --no-ff feature/<task-slug>` — keeps full commit history inside each merge bubble
- Do not squash unless the user explicitly asks
- Do not use one long-lived branch for all roadmap features

